    "body": "**Automated review**: 5 low findings on `fb82fbcd` are collected in #19. They do not hold this pull request; a push that is needed anyway fixes them too.\n\n<!-- kurz-review:findings [{\"file\": \"reference/12-errors.md\", \"line\": 134, \"severity\": \"low\", \"title\": \"The new `index-out-of-range` clause says \\\"a count below 0\\\" where S3 means `max`\", \"sha\": \"fb82fbcd5dcbdc39dd0b0fb1acceed0f18d7a139\"}, {\"file\": \"reference/13-files.md\", \"line\": 187, \"severity\": \"low\", \"title\": \"S6 omits the permissions and close-on-exec of a file that `WriteAll` creates\", \"sha\": \"fb82fbcd5dcbdc39dd0b0fb1acceed0f18d7a139\"}, {\"file\": \"reference/06-values.md\", \"line\": 606, \"severity\": \"low\", \"title\": \"M9 leaves the naming of the standard library open beyond files and sockets, which excludes `Clear`\", \"sha\": \"fb82fbcd5dcbdc39dd0b0fb1acceed0f18d7a139\"}, {\"file\": \"runtime/linux/linux.kz\", \"line\": 1557, \"severity\": \"low\", \"title\": \"Blast radius leaves out the corpus and its runner's lists\", \"sha\": \"fb82fbcd5dcbdc39dd0b0fb1acceed0f18d7a139\"}, {\"file\": \"runtime/linux/linux.kz\", \"line\": 1696, \"severity\": \"low\", \"title\": \"Each thread's page for `stat` is mapped and never freed, so every thread that asks about a file leaks 4096 bytes\", \"sha\": \"fb82fbcd5dcbdc39dd0b0fb1acceed0f18d7a139\"}] -->",
